      </div>

    </div>
    <!-- END WIDGET -->

    <!-- CONTEXT BELOW -->
    <div class="r" style="margin-top:80px;padding-top:48px;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08)">
      <div class="cx-eyebrow">What Affects the Final Cost</div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2rem);color:var(--pure);margin:16px 0 32px">Five things that move the number.</h2>
      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2px">
        <div style="background:#1a1a1a;padding:28px 24px">
          <div style="font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);margin-bottom:10px">Existing Conditions</div>
          <p style="font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--gray2);margin:0">Shell condition, existing MEP rough-in, asbestos abatement requirements, and structural constraints all materially affect cost. A site visit is the only way to know.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#1a1a1a;padding:28px 24px">
          <div style="font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);margin-bottom:10px">Plumbing &amp; Mechanical</div>
          <p style="font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--gray2);margin:0">Adding washrooms, kitchen plumbing, medical gas, or HVAC rezoning adds significant cost that square-footage estimates do not capture until scope is defined.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#1a1a1a;padding:28px 24px">
          <div style="font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);margin-bottom:10px">Custom Millwork</div>
          <p style="font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--gray2);margin:0">Reception counters, boardroom cabinetry, full-wall built-ins, and custom shelving can add $15,000–$100,000+ to a project regardless of square footage.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#1a1a1a;padding:28px 24px">
          <div style="font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);margin-bottom:10px">Permit &amp; Regulatory Scope</div>
          <p style="font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--gray2);margin:0">Change-of-use permits, healthcare occupancy requirements, accessibility upgrades, and fire code compliance work can add 10–25% to a baseline estimate.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#1a1a1a;padding:28px 24px">
          <div style="font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);margin-bottom:10px">Timeline Pressure</div>
          <p style="font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--gray2);margin:0">Fast-track delivery with extended hours and weekend work typically adds 10–20% to the base project cost. We quote this transparently upfront.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="background:#1a1a1a;padding:28px 24px">
          <div style="font-size:.65rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--red);margin-bottom:10px">Electrical Upgrades</div>
          <p style="font-size:.87rem;line-height:1.65;color:var(--gray2);margin:0">Panel upgrades, specialty equipment circuits, and high-density data infrastructure are common sources of cost that do not show in a simple per-square-foot range.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

